{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1200","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. White Lines"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Gildong has bought a famous painting software "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cfpaint"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The working screen of cfpaint is square-shaped consisting of $$$n$$$ rows and $$$n$$$ columns of square cells. The rows are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$, from top to bottom, and the columns are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$, from left to right. The position of a cell at row $$$r$$$ and column $$$c$$$ is represented as $$$(r, c)$$$. There are only two colors for the cells in cfpaint — black and white."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is a tool named "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"eraser"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in cfpaint. The eraser has an integer size $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\le n$$$). To use the eraser, Gildong needs to click on a cell $$$(i, j)$$$ where $$$1 \\le i, j \\le n - k + 1$$$. When a cell $$$(i, j)$$$ is clicked, all of the cells $$$(i', j')$$$ where $$$i \\le i' \\le i + k - 1$$$ and $$$j \\le j' \\le j + k - 1$$$ become white. In other words, a square with side equal to $$$k$$$ cells and top left corner at $$$(i, j)$$$ is colored white."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"white line"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a row or a column without any black cells."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Gildong has worked with cfpaint for some time, so some of the cells (possibly zero or all) are currently black. He wants to know the maximum number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"white lines"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" after using the eraser "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly once"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Help Gildong find the answer to his question."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\le n \\le 2000$$$) — the number of rows and columns, and the size of the eraser."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next $$$n$$$ lines contain $$$n$$$ characters each without spaces. The $$$j$$$-th character in the $$$i$$$-th line represents the cell at $$$(i,j)$$$. Each character is given as either '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' representing a black cell, or '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"W"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' representing a white cell."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer: the maximum number of white lines after using the eraser exactly once."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 2\nBWWW\nWBBW\nWBBW\nWWWB\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 1\nBWB\nWWB\nBWB\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 3\nBWBBB\nBWBBB\nBBBBB\nBBBBB\nWBBBW\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 2\nBW\nWB\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 1\nWW\nWW\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, Gildong can click the cell $$$(2, 2)$$$, then the working screen becomes: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"BWWW\nWWWW\nWWWW\nWWWB\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then there are four white lines — the $$$2$$$-nd and $$$3$$$-rd row, and the $$$2$$$-nd and $$$3$$$-rd column."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, clicking the cell $$$(2, 3)$$$ makes the $$$2$$$-nd row a white line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, both the $$$2$$$-nd column and $$$5$$$-th row become white lines by clicking the cell $$$(3, 2)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1200D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1200/problem/D"}